 "interpretations": [
  "1. R1's attributable excess e_c = |delta1_c| - |deltap_c| is compared with 0.5 sigma_c per cell; a cell is named when e_c > 0.5 sigma_c, and equality stays on the licensed side (§4: 'max_c e_c <= 0.5 sigma_c' licenses, 'some e_c > 0.5 sigma_c' does not)",
  "2. R4 reads each closure against its family's common truth: b = X / X_true - 1 on the 16 cells (RSN rev 3 §3.3), and a change is the difference of two such biases; the reader refuses a family whose truths differ",
  "3. R4 at the prior (J7 ruling): the attributable change is the SIGNED residual [b(X1c) - b(X0c)] - [b(X1pc) - b(X0c)] per cell, W-classed; it is the algebra conservative against licensing, so a null larger than the change, or equal and opposite, is flagged; the stored vector is the one classed",
  "4. R4 at the A7 GiBUU hybrid and the q3 tilt: no refit null was declared there, so the change b(X1) - b(X0) is read in full as the attributable change",
  "5. R4's X1wc - X1c (the weight at the prior) is a qualifier beside R2, not one of the outcome's 'attributable changes at all three truths' (J7 ruling); it is never silent: the outcome record always carries its class and largest |change|/sigma, and states in words when it crosses R2's threshold (some cell beyond 0.5 sigma)",
  "6. R3's difference is t_c(X1t) - t_c(X0t) at the last iteration, T-classed as each transfer is; a cell with no masked rows in either is None and fails T0 and T1, as in RSN"
 ],
